# State management

- UI state: `sealed class XState extends Equatable` with variants `Loading`, `Loaded`, `Failed` (pattern: `readiness_state.dart`).
- Use `part 'x_state.dart';` on the cubit when state is colocated.
- Emit immutable state; put derived flags on `Loaded` (e.g. `canRecord`), not parallel boolean fields on the cubit.
- Map errors to user-safe messages via `Failure` (`core/errors/failures.dart`), then `emit(ReadinessFailed(message))`.
- No platform channels or `RecliteEngine` inside cubits — only repositories.
- Local UI only (tab index, animation): `StatefulWidget` + `setState` is fine; feature data belongs in a cubit.

```dart
// BAD — missing exhaustiveness, magic string error
if (state is ReadinessLoaded) { ... }

// GOOD — home_page.dart
switch (state) {
  ReadinessLoading() => ...,
  ReadinessFailed(:final message) => _FailedView(message: message),
  final ReadinessLoaded loaded => _LoadedView(state: loaded),
}
```